      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is March 24, 2026, from 02:00 to 04:00 local time. If validation checks fail during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to run the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior ruleset and replays the invalidation hook. After rollback, the team must notify Verdant Bay, open an incident for manual remediation, and revert any partial replays. This rollback is automatic if any validation fails during the patch validation phase, which includes running synthetic approval flows and sampling in-flight approvals. The rollback command and post-rollback steps are part of the emergency playbook for Verdant Bay's policy evaluation order fix [art_fff67d92fe41], [art_f893faeda15a]. \n\nNote that the evidence does not provide more detailed step-by-step commands beyond the single CLI rollback command, nor does it enumerate the exact validation check criteria beyond \"if any validation fails.\"",
