      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical PoC of NoiseGuard, a low-mid pricing competitor offering tactical noise reduction. Pioneer Freight Solutions is at high retention risk if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, as procurement is likely to extend NoiseGuard and reduce scope with Northstar [art_ac8afb52f2d3].\n\nThe exact milestone at risk for Pioneer Freight Solutions is the acceptance of the remediation plan for the taxonomy change incident. The acceptance criteria for this milestone include precision@10 \u2265 0.8 for facility lookups, entity-link hit rate \u2265 90%, and grouping false positives \u2264 5%. The milestone acceptance window is from 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-14, following backfill and recomputation of index weights scheduled from 2026-04-12 to 2026-04-30 [art_7373b64fdfdd].\n\nRegarding other customers mentioned in the evidence\u2014FrostGrid Energi AB, Nordic MedSupply AB, NorrLog Freight AB, and Fyrkrona Renewables AB\u2014there is no explicit evidence identifying them as likely to defect to cheaper tactical competitors if milestones are missed, nor explicit confirmation of milestone details for them. These customers face competition from EdgeCollector Co. (FrostGrid Energi AB, Nordic MedSupply AB, NorrLog Freight AB) and Patchway (Fyrkrona Renewables AB), but the evidence does not specify milestone risks or retention threats tied to missed milestones for these accounts [art_8e8c5e2be8ee, art_fe23391b438f, art_b50b72e5837c, art_599ab3ce9cc8].\n\nIn summary, Pioneer Freight Solutions is the only customer explicitly identified as at high risk of defection to a cheaper tactical competitor (NoiseGuard) if the next milestone is missed, and the milestone is the acceptance of the remediation plan for the taxonomy change incident with acceptance criteria and dates as detailed above [art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd]. No similar risk or milestone details are confirmed for other customers in the evidence.",
